      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cefditoren, a third-generation cephalosporin, is the oral β-lactam more active against the main community-acquired respiratory tract pathogens (including resistance phenotypes such as penicillin-resistant Streptococcus pneumoniae and ampicillin-resistant Haemophilus influenzae), similar to cefotaxime. Data obtained from clinical trials and later evidence on efficacy and safety, support that cefditoren is an suitable option for the treatment of mild-to moderate community respiratory and urinary tract infections, particularly in regions where non-susceptible phenotipes to common oral antibiotics are prevalent."},
